<title>SINGAPORE: Pentex-Schweizer 1st-half net falls.</title>
<headline>Pentex-Schweizer 1st-half net falls.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				4.15 vs   7.60</p>
<p>    Dividend (percent)		    4.00 vs   5.00</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		     6.22 vs  11.40</p>
<p>    Group shr fully diluted (cents)   6.17 vs  11.34</p>
<p>    Turnover				 39.05 vs  50.54</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	 0.22 vs   0.21</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		    0.09 vs   0.33</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortisation	   3.47 vs   3.78</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			  5.14 vs   9.77</p>
<p>    Tax					 0.99 vs   2.17</p>
<p>    Dividend pay date:   April 29, 1997</p>
<p>Last day books open: April 14, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Pentex-Schweizer Circuits Ltd makes printed circuit boards for the electronics industry.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
